1.ls => List files in the current directory
2.ls  <dir>  => List files in <dir>
3.ls -l => List files with details
4.ls -a => List all files (including hidden)
5.ls -al => List all files with details
6.pwd => Print the current/working
directory
7.cd  <dir> =>  Change current directory to
<dir>
8.cd ..=>  Go up one directory
9.mkdir <dir> => Create directory
10.mkdir -p  <dir> => Create directory and any missing
parent directories
11.cp -r <src> <dst> => Copy a directory and its contents
12.mv <src> <dst> => Move / rename a directory
13.rmdir <dir> => Remove an empty directory
